  "name": "Trobamuffin (Occitan raggamuffin)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Occitan-language ragga developed in Marseille from the mid-1980s by Massilia Sound System, whose members named it trobamuffin, joining Jamaican sound-system toasting to the troubadour heritage and to Provençal Occitan and Marseille street speech. Its songs on local identity, politics and fêtes were carried by self-organised sound-system parties and concerts, and in Toulouse the Fabulous Trobadors developed a related Occitan chatted-verse style.",
